SPU: an indirect branch to a lifted function skips the resolver's special cases (12 -> 6.5 ns per indirect step).

Lifted SPU code reaches every computed target (bi, a return through a register) through spu_indirect_branch. The
resolver tests a dozen special cases one by one inside a large frame (interrupt return, SPURS kernel services, the
job-return address, the taskset's task region, diagnostic variables) before and after the lookup, and none applies
to almost any target. In a Resistance 3 firefight (v0.17.0) the resolver and its helpers were a large part of the
~10.5% of the SPU threads' time the trampoline steps took.

spu_indirect_branch first checks that none of the special cases can apply (no interrupt return pending, not one of
their addresses, no task registered above the task region, no diagnostic variable set), takes the dispatch cache's
hit inline and tail-calls the target; anything else goes to the unchanged resolver (spu_indirect_branch_full) from
the top. (The step-check half of this patch on v0.17.0 is upstream since v0.18.0: #434.) A hit on relocatable code
(#636) restores ctx->reloc_delta, as spu_lifted_lookup's own hit does.

Test: runtime/spu/tests/test_spu_lifted_start.c, test_indirect_fast_path_guards: a lifted function registered at
each special address (interrupt return, exit-to-kernel, selectWorkload, job return, a task entry, below the task
region) must not run in its place; each guard left out fails its check. test_indirect_fast_path_reloc: relocatable
code reached through the fast path runs with its placement's delta on cache hits too (fails without the restore).
No header changes: the module ABI is the same.
Micro-benchmark on v0.18.0 (a function re-queued through spu_drain_call through spu_indirect_branch to one of 256
registered targets, 3 runs): 12.0-12.7 -> 6.4-6.9 ns per step; direct steps unchanged.
On v0.17.0 in the game (`sample`, 25 s of the Haven firefight, 3 runs each), with the step check: the trampoline
functions 10.4-10.6% -> 7.6-8.2% of the SPU threads' time.

Upstream: not proposed yet.
---

diff --git a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
index d91d1007..2a29f76c 100644
--- a/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_channels.c
@@ -1857,2 +1857,13 @@ static void spu_dcache_shadow_stats(void)
 }
